{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"snapshot_suffix_monotonic_successor.json\", \"summary\": \"Two things this turn. First, the previous verdict was accepted: the successor experiment's interpretation is recorded (`conclusion: violated`, receipt 2322bd7884b749f89c3101f04bc82e78, decisive indices [1,3]) and the investigation is marked `explained` — the primary defect is fully sourced, executed and concluded.\\n\\nSecond, a new discriminator probe is submitted as a successor (previous_id set, with revision reason). Question: is the catch-up stall caused by the retained above-snapshot log *bytes* or by the cached last-log *state*? `installSnapshot` already takes the `removeOldLogs` branch for a `MonotonicLogStore` (raft.go:1814-1953), which deletes all logs up to the snapshot's last index, so if the stall were byte-driven it should not occur there. The probe runs the same scenario three ways in one execution — control (log below snapshot index, non-monotonic), non-monotonic stall, and monotonic stall (`MakeClusterCustom` with `MonotonicLogs: true`) — and asserts `stalled == false` under `stale_suffix == true` for both store types.\\n\\nLocal native feedback (not the formal receipt): the monotonic case stalls exactly like the non-monotonic one — `snapshot_index=45`, `old_last_before=222`, `old_last_after=223`, `old_applied_after=45`, `leader_commit_index=55`, `stalled=true` — even though `removeOldLogs` emptied the store. The node's `LastIndex()` still reports 223, so the cause is the cached `lastLogIndex/lastLogTerm` that `installSnapshot` never resets (no `setLastLog` call), read by `getLastEntry` (state.go:167-174) and rejected by the `PrevLogEntry` check (raft.go:1475-1502). The control still converges (holds), so this is not a blanket snapshot failure. Envelope validates (`valid: true`); the experiment needs its own receipt before it can carry an interpretation. Draft file: `draft/snapshot_suffix_monotonic_successor.json` (harness: `draft/snapshot_suffix_harness_monotonic.go`).\"}"}}
